[LTO] Find the global symbols that inline asm in function bodies defines

ModuleSymbolTable only parsed module level asm, so a symbol defined by inline
asm inside a function was unknown to the linker. The symbol is missing from the
symbol table, so references to it are reported undefined, and the function
holding the asm is deleted by LTO as dead because nothing in the IR calls it.
wine defines the RTTI symbols of its C++ runtime emulation this way, and its
PE build cannot use LTO because of it.

Parse the inline asm of each call whose string contains .glob or .weak,
standing in 0 for the operands, which are not known here, and honouring the
dialect alternatives. Global definitions and references are reported like those
of module asm, and the function that defines a symbol is flagged used in the
irsymtab so ThinLTO and regular LTO keep it. Its summary is marked noinline so
the asm is not copied. Regular LTO reads the bodies of a lazily loaded module
when its irsymtab has symbols the module does not show without them.

